A bustling Asian convenience store backroom rendered in Vincent van Gogh's expressive post-impressionist style, with swirling brushstrokes of deep blues, warm yellows, and vibrant oranges. Shelves filled with colorful inventory boxes curve and dance with characteristic Van Gogh energy. In the foreground, a smartphone lies on a wooden crate, its screen glowing with soft light, reflecting off nearby product packages. The scene captures the chaotic beauty of inventory management transformed into art—cardboard boxes stacked in spiraling formations, price tags fluttering like starry night elements, and the warm glow of overhead storage lights creating halos of thick, textured paint strokes. Fresh spring rolls (popiah) sit in a small basket nearby, a subtle nod to the namesake. The entire composition pulses with movement and life, transforming mundane stockroom work into something magical and dynamic.
